      "description": "This is a map of Matagorda Bay, Texas as of 1689.  The map was drawn by Carlos de Sigüenza y Góngora based on sketches compiled during the expedition of Alonso de Leon.  The Spanish called the bay \"Lago de San Bernardo\". An F marks the spot of the French settlement, Fort Saint Louis, and \"Navio Quebrado\", or \"broken ship\", marks the spot where the French ship La Belle was grounded.",
